# Line endings are pinned here instead of being left to each contributor's
# core.autocrlf. A CRLF checkout of a shipped hook is not cosmetic: bash reads
# `then\r` as a command, so the hook dies mid-verdict and every tool call it
# gates is denied with a syntax error (probe-verified: exit 2).
*.sh                        text eol=lf
plugin/bin/oso-state        text eol=lf
plugin/git-hooks/pre-commit text eol=lf

# The Windows entrypoints pin what already ships: both files are LF in this tree
# today, so LF is the form that has actually been exercised. CRLF would be the
# conventional Windows choice, but switching would ship a form nothing here has
# run — and bootstrap/verify.sh check 11 scans both for CR bytes either way.
*.ps1                       text eol=lf
*.bat                       text eol=lf

# The two data files the bootstrap READS, pinned for the same class of reason
# one layer up. A trailing CR on a gentle-manifest.txt line makes every
# `[ -e "$CLAUDE_DIR/$rel" ]` test miss, so the legacy cleanup removes nothing,
# announces 0 and is confirmed removed by verify.sh — three layers agreeing over
# a cleanup that never ran. claude-global.md is copied verbatim into the
# operator's always-loaded CLAUDE.md, whose budget check counts every byte it
# would gain. Neither pin is the whole fix: .gitattributes renormalizes no clone
# that already exists, so the manifest's three readers drop the CR themselves.
bootstrap/gentle-manifest.txt text eol=lf
bootstrap/claude-global.md    text eol=lf
